    "updated_at": "2015-11-25T13:38:18Z",
    "body": "> The microformats wiki is where rel=tag was originally specified.\n\nThat's interesting, but not really related to my question.\n\nHTML does not contain semantics for treating path segments as \"the tag\". If microformats adds new semantics on top of HTML, it is of course free to add more restrictions to go along with those additional semantics. One such semantic might be requiring that `<a rel=\"tag\">` instances use a subset of URL syntax, instead of allowing any URL like all other `<a>`s do. But for HTML, it seems more appropriate to use standard URL syntax restrictions (and, as @annevk points out, to use the canonical Wikipedia URLs, instead of ones that redirect to the canonical URL).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
